Add missing <map> includes for libc++.

These device_*.hpp headers use std::map (via the Argument/Invoker string
helpers) without including <map>, relying on it arriving transitively through
libstdc++'s <iostream>. libc++ does not provide it that way, so the build
fails there.

Regenerated from composable-kernel-7.0.1-libcxx-includes.patch for ROCm 10.0:
the original covered 42 headers; one
(device_gemm_xdl_cshuffle_streamk_v3.hpp) no longer exists at 10.0 and is
dropped, the remaining 41 all still lack the include. Generated mechanically
by inserting after the existing <iostream>/<iterator> include, matching the
original's placement. verified 2026-08-29.
